DESCRIPTION:Electric Contrasts: The Art of the Detail brings together phot
 obooks and magazines to show how the revolution of photography in the late
  19th and early 20th century changed the history of art. Electric Contrast
 s takes Kenneth Clark’s landmark 1938 book One Hundred Details from Pict
 ures in the National Gallery as a starting point to illuminate the impact 
 black and white photographic details of Old Master paintings had on new wa
 ys of seeing in the early 20th century. The exhibition reveals the ana\n\n
 Ages: All ages\nLast synced: 2026-10-24 09:28 PDT
LOCATION:McMurtry Building
END:VEVENT
