 26-10-28T10:00:00-07:00@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Deepfakes are getting harder to spot and easier to create. Wha
 t began largely as a reputational and political concern is quickly becomin
 g an operational business risk\, with companies confronting executive impe
 rsonation\, financial fraud\, fake job candidates\, fabricated evidence\, 
 and new threats to identity and authentication. \nDrawing on a session fir
 st presented at Stanford Directors’ College\, Breon Peace\, Partner at C
 leary Gottlieb\, and Douglas Levin\, Executive Fellow at Harvard Business 
 School\n\nAges: All ages\nSource: https://law.stanford.edu/event/deepfakes
 -what-boards-executives-need-to-know/\nLast synced: 2026-10-24 09:28 PDT
