SUMMARY:[Stanford Law] Superjustice: What AI in Tax Reveals About the Futu
 re of Law
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261117T125000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261117T140000
DTSTAMP:20261024T162810Z
UID:stanford_campus-law-10003357-1794919800-1794924000@law.stanford.edu-20
 26-11-17T12:50:00-08:00@local-events
DESCRIPTION:What changes when AI moves from answering legal questions to h
 elping carry out legal work? Using tax as a concrete case study\, Benjamin
  Alarie examines the transition from AI-assisted research toward systems t
 hat support planning\, implementation\, and auditing. Drawing on his exper
 ience building Blue J and on Superjustice: Law in the Age of Artificial In
 telligence (Oxford University Press\, 2026)\, co-authored with Samuel I. B
 echer\, he explores what this transition means for professional judgment\,
 \n\nAges: All ages\nSource: https://law.stanford.edu/event/superjustice-wh
 at-ai-in-tax-reveals-about-the-future-of-law/\nLast synced: 2026-10-24 09:
 28 PDT
